From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:18:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] phy: samsung-ufs: Add Tensor G4 calibration data

Add Tensor G4 PMA calibration, per-lane calibration-done polling and PMU
isolation data using the existing Samsung UFS PHY framework. The 36 PMA
settings come from Google's GPL zuma calibration tables, whose EVT0 and
EVT1 values agree; retain Samsung's source attribution. Convert byte
offsets to the word units used by the common configuration macros.

Returning -ETIMEDOUT after the 4 ms calibration wait is deliberate.
Google's __UFS_CAL_FW__ path returns a timeout, but its kernel build
continues after 100 polls of 40 us. Fail link startup when calibration
does not complete instead of using an unqualified PHY.

The driver data matches the private Pixel 9a bring-up source that
reached internal UFS and guarded native root on two equalised-firmware
boots. This series does not enable board nodes or qualify
suspend/resume.

Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/ufs/zuma/ufs-cal.h
Link: https://android.googlesource.com/kernel/google-modules/soc/gs/+/204078758737776959ecc85c527a00fd2cabb62f/drivers/ufs/zuma/ufs-cal-if.c
Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
